     fhir:div [ fhir:v "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem artemis-prototype-devices-cs</b></p><a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs\"> </a><a name=\"hcartemis-prototype-devices-cs\"> </a><p><b>Properties</b></p><p><b>This code system defines the following properties for its concepts</b></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Type</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td></tr><tr><td>deviceType</td><td>deviceType</td><td>string</td><td>Device category (suit, life-support, habitat, communications, navigation, medical-equipment, rover, drone, logistics, isru, power)</td></tr><tr><td>testEnvironment</td><td>testEnvironment</td><td>string</td><td>Primary test environment (ground, iss, analog-mission)</td></tr><tr><td>manufacturer</td><td>manufacturer</td><td>string</td><td>Device manufacturer or contractor</td></tr></table><p><b>Concepts</b></p><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>https://awatson1978.github.io/aerospace-medicine-ig/CodeSystem/artemis-prototype-devices-cs</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td><td><b>deviceType</b></td><td><b>testEnvironment</b></td><td><b>manufacturer</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">xemu-demo<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-xemu-demo\"> </a></td><td>xEMU Demo Unit</td><td>Prototype EVA suit used in ground testing or ISS demonstration (not flight-certified). Test env: ground.</td><td>suit</td><td>ground</td><td/></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">nextgen-plss<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-nextgen-plss\"> </a></td><td>Next-Generation PLSS</td><td>Next-generation Portable Life Support System under development (for suits beyond Artemis). Test env: ground.</td><td>life-support</td><td>ground</td><td/></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">biomonitor-wearable<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-biomonitor-wearable\"> </a></td><td>BioMonitor Wearable Prototype</td><td>Experimental biomedical monitoring device (advanced smart garment for astronauts in trial). Test env: ISS.</td><td>medical-equipment</td><td>iss</td><td/></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">autonomous-medical-unit<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-autonomous-medical-unit\"> </a></td><td>Autonomous Medical Unit Prototype</td><td>Prototype diagnostic device or smart medical assistant being evaluated for lunar use. Test env: ground.</td><td>medical-equipment</td><td>ground</td><td/></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">habitat-test-module<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-habitat-test-module\"> </a></td><td>Habitat Test Module</td><td>Ground-based habitat prototype (e.g., 3D-printed habitat analog or Lunar/Mars yard modules). Test env: analog-mission.</td><td>habitat</td><td>analog-mission</td><td/></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">surface-habitat-module<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-surface-habitat-module\"> </a></td><td>Surface Habitat Module</td><td>Planned lunar surface habitat infrastructure element. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>habitat</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">pressurized-rover-proto<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-pressurized-rover-proto\"> </a></td><td>Pressurized Rover Prototype</td><td>Early concept lunar pressurized rover (testing life support and habitat functions on Earth). Test env: ground.</td><td>rover</td><td>ground</td><td/></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">crewed-ltv<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-crewed-ltv\"> </a></td><td>Crewed LTV</td><td>Crewed Lunar Terrain Vehicle variant under development. Manufacturer: NASA / Industry Team. Test env: ground.</td><td>rover</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Industry Team</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">uncrewed-ltv<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-uncrewed-ltv\"> </a></td><td>Uncrewed LTV</td><td>Uncrewed (teleoperated) Lunar Terrain Vehicle variant under development. Manufacturer: NASA / Industry Team. Test env: ground.</td><td>rover</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Industry Team</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">advanced-ltv<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-advanced-ltv\"> </a></td><td>Advanced LTV</td><td>Advanced Lunar Terrain Vehicle concept. Manufacturer: NASA / Industry Team. Test env: ground.</td><td>rover</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Industry Team</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">ltv-gen-2<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-ltv-gen-2\"> </a></td><td>LTV Generation 2</td><td>Second-generation Lunar Terrain Vehicle concept. Manufacturer: NASA / Industry Team. Test env: ground.</td><td>rover</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Industry Team</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">excavator-rover<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-excavator-rover\"> </a></td><td>Excavator Rover</td><td>Lunar surface excavation rover under development. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>rover</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">site-prep-logistics-rover<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-site-prep-logistics-rover\"> </a></td><td>Site Preparation and Logistics Rover</td><td>Rover concept for site preparation and logistics tasks. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>rover</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">international-partner-rover<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-international-partner-rover\"> </a></td><td>International Partner Rover</td><td>Partner-provided lunar rover under development. Manufacturer: International Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>rover</td><td>ground</td><td>International Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">science-rover<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-science-rover\"> </a></td><td>Science Rover</td><td>Lunar surface science rover concept. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: analog-mission.</td><td>rover</td><td>analog-mission</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">moonfall-drone<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-moonfall-drone\"> </a></td><td>MoonFall Drone</td><td>Lunar surface aerial or descent support drone concept. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>drone</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">orbital-comm-relay<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-orbital-comm-relay\"> </a></td><td>Orbital Communication Relay</td><td>Orbital relay satellite for lunar communications. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>communications</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">observation-satellite<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-observation-satellite\"> </a></td><td>Observation Satellite</td><td>Lunar observation and monitoring satellite. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>communications</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">relay-satellite-observability<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-relay-satellite-observability\"> </a></td><td>Relay Satellite with Observability</td><td>Relay satellite with observability functions. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>communications</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">surface-comm-nav-node<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-surface-comm-nav-node\"> </a></td><td>Surface Communication and Navigation Node</td><td>Lunar surface communication and navigation infrastructure node. Manufacturer: NASA / Partners. Test env: ground.</td><td>communications</td><td>ground</td><td>NASA / Partners</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">deployable-surface-comm-tower<a name=\"artemis-prototype-devices-cs-deployable-surface-comm-tower\